  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JPD 2021-2023 - JPD 2021-2023, 2018-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">JPD 2021-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sverige har &#xe5;tagit sig att bidra till genomf&#xf6;randet av Agenda 2030 genom personella resurser till EU:s delegationer runt om i v&#xe4;rlden. F&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; detta st&#xf6;djer Sida Junior Professionals in Delegation (JPD-programmet), och genom programmet placeras 17 svenska JPD p&#xe5; delegationer f&#xf6;r att bidra till EEAS eller Europeiska Kommissionens verksamhet.

Insatsen g&#xe4;ller finansiering av femton (15) svenska traineer till EU:s traineeprogram Junior Professionals in Delegation under perioden 2021-2023. I till&#xe4;gg till de femton traineer som finansieras av Sida kommer ytterligare tv&#xe5; svenska traineer att delta i programmet under samma period. Dessa tv&#xe5; finansieras av EEAS och Europeiska Kommissionen.

JPD inneb&#xe4;r en personell f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkning till mottagande delegation och JPD f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas bidra inom de arbetsomr&#xe5;den som aktuell delegation arbetar med: implementering av program (EC-placeringar) liksom politisk bevakning/rapportering (EEAS-placeringar). En JPD kan arbeta inom samtliga tematiska omr&#xe5;den som delegationen &#xe4;r verksam inom.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sweden is committed to contribute to the implementation of Agenda 2030 in low- and middle income countries by providing human resources to work with and through the diverse mandates of EU Delegations. For this purpose, Sweden closely collaborates with the EEAS regarding placements in EEAS and European Commission delegations around the world through the Junior Professionals in Delegation program (JPD). Through the program, 17 Swedish JPD&apos;s will be placed at EU delegations to contribute to the EEAS and EC activities.

The contribution regards the financing of fifteen (15) Swedish trainees to the EU trainee programme Junior Professionals in Delegation during 2021-2023. In addition to the fifteen trainees financed by Sida another two Swedish trainees will, financed by the European Union External Action (EEAS) and the European Commission, participate in the program.

JPD:s are often viewed as a regular staff member and are, as such, expected to contribute to regular operations. For EC JPD:s this may entail program implementation, while for EEAS JPD:s focus is mainly on political/press function. A JPD may work with all thematic areas that the delegation operates within.</narrative>
  </description>
